{"id":"chatcmpl-4ed1e79a-0625-4fc5-ba1e-2d30399c047a","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250900,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When multiple independent visual-question-answering models disagree on a subtle radiological finding, the task is resolved by (1) querying several models for the same targeted attribute, (2) using the forced-choice structure of the question as a prior that a positive finding exists, and (3) escalating to region-of-interest inspection and expert-focused re-reading when models conflict. The winning strategy treats model disagreement as a signal to gather more evidence rather than to default to the majority 'negative' answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Query multiple independent models for the same specific attribute (presence + laterality) so that disagreement itself becomes diagnostic information.\",\n    \"Exploit the forced-choice framing: if the question presupposes a finding exists, treat 'no finding' model outputs as likely false negatives on subtle cases.\",\n    \"Escalate from whole-image model queries to targeted region-of-interest crops and expert re-reads when models conflict, rather than trusting a single modality.\",\n    \"Decompose the decision into the discriminating attribute (here, left vs. right side) and direct every tool query at that attribute to maximize comparability.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"medical imaging QA\": \"Ask each model the same narrow question (presence + side/location); use conflicts to trigger ROI crops and expert-focused re-reads; weight any positive finding over unanimous negatives when the prompt implies a finding exists.\",\n    \"multi-model consensus tasks\": \"Collect independent opinions on the same attribute, then resolve disagreement by adding higher-resolution or expert evidence rather than simple majority voting.\",\n    \"forced-choice visual QA\": \"Treat the option set as a prior: eliminate options only with positive counter-evidence, and prefer the option supported by at least one credible source over 'none of the above' reasoning.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm every model was asked the identical discriminating question (presence + laterality) so outputs are directly comparable.\",\n    \"Before finalizing, verify the chosen option is supported by at least one positive source and that conflicting negatives were addressed via ROI or expert re-read.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":843,"total_tokens":1284,"completion_tokens":441,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":843},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":441}}}